  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3007.03 Substitution of NOx for VOCs Reductions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3007.03 Substitution of NOx for VOCs Reductions. ERCs certified for reductions of nitrogen oxides (NOx), shall be eligible to satisfy any applicable requirements for volatile organic compounds (VOCs). Substitution of NOx for VOCs reductions shall be in a ratio of 1:1, or an alternative ratio approved by the division and EPA. Such proposed substitution shall be consistent with the modeling analyses contained in the SIP; and each proposed substitution shall be required to be supported by a modeling analysis specific to such use that demonstrates that the proposed substitution does not violate any applicable requirement of the National Emissions Standards for Hazardous Air Pollutants (NESHAPS) or Env-A 1300 or Env-A 1400.\n\nSource. #6441, EXEMPT, eff 1-21-97",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a3000.html"
}
